{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Dinner for Four", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Time for a Diet", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 10, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 3, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": " Identify and describe personal and regional eating habits and cooking in a range of communicative situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn6le03ob10re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Expressing Quantities and Amounts", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "The most usual words used to express quantity in English are <span class=\"strong\">much</span> and <span class=\"strong\">many</span>.<br>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">much</span> with <span class=\"italic\">non-count nouns</span> to refer to an amount:<br><br> <span class=\"strong\">Examples:</span><br> <span class=\"italic\">There is so much to say about the new film!<br>\u2028How much time do you have this week?<br>\u2028There isn't much  food in the house.</span><br><br>You use <span class=\"strong\">many</span> with <span class=\"italic\">count nouns</span> to refer to a number:<br><br> <span class=\"strong\">Examples:</span><br> <span class=\"italic\">Many people prefer winter vacations.<br>\u2028How many books on archaeology do you have?<br>\u2028There aren't many apples in the fridge.</span><br><br> The following expressions are also used with <span class=\"italic\">count nouns</span> and <span class=\"italic\">non-count nouns</span>  <br><br> a lot of<br>\u2028lots of<br>\u2028plenty of<br>\u2028a great deal of<br>\u2028a large number of<br>\u2028the majority of<br>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I eat too much fast food.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I had too many slices of pizza last night.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I must drink a lot of water.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Saying what is NOT necessary", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use \"<span class=\"strong\">Don't have to</span>\" or \"<span class=\"strong\">Doesn't have to</span>\" to express what is not necessary. <br/>Remember to use a verb in its base form after \"<span class=\"strong\">Don't</span>/<span class=\"strong\">Doesn't have to</span>\".", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Structure:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":1,\"columns\":5,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Subject <br/>You/We/I/They <br/>She/He </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">+ auxiliary in negative<br/><span class=\\\"strong\\\">don't <br/>doesn't</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"+  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">have</span> to\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"+ verb in base form (infinitive)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"+ complement\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "You <span class=\"strong\">don't</span> <span class=\"italic\">have</span> to eat just a little bit or eat only salads. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "She <span class=\"strong\">doesn't</span> <span class=\"italic\">have</span> to watch her portions.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "healthy", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to eat food or live in a way that's good for your health ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You have to stop eating so much if you want to be healthy.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le03ob10aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you hear/use when talking about diets.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to gain weight", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a more polite way to talk about increase in weight", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Sally would have to eat more nutritious foods to not gain weight.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le03ob10aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "protein", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a substance found in milk, eggs, meat and beans that helps the body to grow and be strong ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Foods with more protein are important to make your muscles strong.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le03ob10aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "fiber", "type": "name"}, {"content": "vegetable material that cannot be digested and helps other food to pass through your body ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Foods with more fiber helps to clear your system.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le03ob10aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "calorie", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a measurement used to indicate the amount of energy that food will produce in the human body ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Each of us should eat enough food to get 1500-2000 calories a day.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le03ob10aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "antioxidant", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a substance contained in certain foods that prevents some chemicals from damaging our body ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Blueberries and broccoli contain a lot of antioxidants.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le03ob10aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to ingest", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to eat or swallow", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Ingesting a lot of deep-fried foods is not healthy.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le03ob10aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Think about everything you eat each day and how your diet can improve. Write down some notes.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write 5 sentences using expressions of necessity on how you plan to make your diet more nutritious.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Be sure to also include quantities and amounts in your sentences.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your new diet plan to your partner.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I apply critical-thinking to my eating habits.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write complete statements on how my diet can improve.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I express necessity and quantities.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I read my new diet plan to my partner.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "type": "scholar", "exercises": [{"id": 0, "stimuli_ids": [0], "questions": [], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can talk about daily routines and eating habits in the present.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can express what is necessary.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about quantities and amounts. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " Have you gone on some kind of diet for health reasons?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " What did you have to do?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": "Correct", "allowed_attempts": 2, "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"conte